From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 22:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] dsound: Keep the high quality resampler for any number of
 buffers.

Staging's dsound-Fast_Mixer switches every resampled buffer to a linear
resampler once more than HQBuffersMax (default 4) buffers exist. That
path reads the live buffer memory, while the no-resample and FIR paths
read the committed region between the play and write cursors (Wine
commit 975d0632a19), so audio a game streams into that region can
glitch.

Liarsoft's codeX RScript games play 44.1 kHz buffers and reach 5 of
them during play, and their BGM crackles after voice lines on a 48 kHz
device. Forcing the device to 44.1 kHz avoids resampling and the
crackle, and Proton and upstream Wine, which only have the FIR path,
don't crackle.

Default HQBuffersMax to INT_MAX so the FIR path is always used, as
upstream. The registry value can still lower it.

https://github.com/GloriousEggroll/proton-ge-custom/issues/521
---
--- a/dlls/dsound/dsound_main.c
+++ b/dlls/dsound/dsound_main.c
@@ -81,7 +81,12 @@
 
 /* All default settings, you most likely don't want to touch these, see wiki on UsefulRegistryKeys */
 int ds_hel_buflen = 32768 * 2;
-int ds_hq_buffers_max = 4;
+/* Staging's linear resampler is used once more than this many buffers exist. It
+ * reads the live buffer instead of the committed region the other mixing paths
+ * use, so streamed audio can glitch when a game rewrites that region. Keep the
+ * high quality resampler for any number of buffers, like upstream Wine; the
+ * HQBuffersMax registry value can still lower it. */
+int ds_hq_buffers_max = 0x7fffffff;
 BOOL ds_eax_enabled = TRUE;
 
 #define IS_OPTION_TRUE(ch) \
